<node id="&quot;PROOF-OF-CONCEPT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Proof-of-concept refers to demonstrations or tests conducted to show how a particular technology or concept, like an AI model, can function or be used in real-world scenarios, which is relevant when assessing risks and safety."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-110a9d0daa1bc9fd14dbe5e0d3884ec7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH-VALUE EXPLOITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High-value exploits are advanced attacks that use AI models to compromise systems, demonstrating the potential risks and the need for robust security measures when deploying such models."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-110a9d0daa1bc9fd14dbe5e0d3884ec7</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HARDENED TARGETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hardened targets are systems that have been fortified to resist various forms of cyber-attacks, indicating a focus on security in the context of evaluating AI models for safety.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-110a9d0daa1bc9fd14dbe5e0d3884ec7</data>
</node>
