  <data key="d2">chunk-0aaba30aa4656afc2913dd441e62ee04</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CRISPR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CRISPR is a gene-editing tool being explored for the treatment and potential cure of HIV, highlighting its scientific significance in medical research."&lt;SEP&gt;"CRISPR is a technology involved in the study and design of treatments for HIV, which has concerns about off-target effects."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HIV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DISEASE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HIV is the disease targeted by the research and EBT-101 treatment, which is central to the study and clinical trial efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIV is the target disease for potential treatment with CRISPR, which is of public health concern with millions affected globally."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNITED NATIONS PROGRAMME ON HIV/AIDS (UNAIDS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"UNAIDS is an organization that tracks and reports data on HIV/AIDS, emphasizing its role in public health communication."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THOMAS HOPE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Thomas Hope is a professor whose expertise contributes to the understanding and discussion of CRISPR's potential in treating diseases like HIV."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELENA HERRERA-CARRILLO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Elena Herrera-Carrillo is an associate professor whose research focuses on using CRISPR to edit cells harboring HIV reservoirs, highlighting her academic contribution to the field."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CARTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MEDICINE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Combination antiretroviral therapies (cARTs) are the cornerstone of HIV treatment, suppressing the virus and extending the lives of those infected, but they are not a cure and require lifelong adherence."&lt;SEP&gt;"cARTs, or combination antiretroviral therapies, are the standard treatment for HIV, which currently suppress the virus but are not a cure."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;KAMEL KAHLILI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Kamel Kahlili is a professor focused on developing EBT-101, which indicates his active role in CRISPR research for HIV treatment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCISION BIOTHERAPEUTICS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Excision BioTherapeutics is the company co-founded by Kamel Kahlili, involved in the development of EBT-101 for treating HIV."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR GENE AND CELL THERAPY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The annual meeting of the European Society for Gene and Cell Therapy is an event where scientific advancements, like the presentation of EBT-101, are shared and discussed among experts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-121134dcc41ea28b3e955f95546eb740</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOPE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Hope is a researcher who studies the mechanisms behind HIV infections at a lab."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;THE LAB&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Lab is the place where Hope conducts research on HIV infections, though its specific name is not mentioned."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OFF-TARGET EFFECTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Off-target effects refer to unintended genetic alterations caused by CRISPR, which is significant for the efficacy and safety of HIV treatments like EBT-101."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EBT-101&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"EBT-101 is the subject of an ongoing clinical trial, a treatment related to CRISPR technology aimed at combating HIV."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-TERM FOLLOW-UP STUDY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Long-term follow-up study is an event designed to monitor participants after receiving EBT-101 to check for any long-term adverse effects over 15 years."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLINICAL TRIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Clinical trial is an event where EBT-101 is being tested for safety, efficacy, and its ability to suppress HIV in patients off cART."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CART THERAPIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"cART therapies refer to antiretroviral treatment protocols used to suppress HIV replication, a key consideration in the clinical trial of EBT-101."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY LIFTING OF TREATMENT BRAKES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporarily lifting the treatment brakes refers to the method used to determine if HIV has been effectively disabled in patients during the clinical trial of EBT-101."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURPOSEFUL TREATMENT INTERRUPTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purposeful treatment interruptions are a deliberate aspect of the clinical trial, necessary to assess remission but debated due to risks involved in discontinuing HIV treatment."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9350df122f7b477c236503a9ef271986</data>
</node>
